================================================================================================
K10-K13  ROUTE (i) -- virial split: the phantom is the pressure part of the cold stress
================================================================================================
K10 PASS 0.0e+00 <1e-25 :: T_00 - (1/2)g_00 T = (rho+3p)/2 exactly ==> laplacian(Phi) = 4 pi G (rho+3p): the active density is rho+3p
K11 PASS 0.0e+00 / 0.0e+00 <1e-25 both :: u = 1+3<w> exactly, <w> volume-weighted: for w(r)=w0 (r/R)^n it is w0/(n+1) -- profile dependent unless w is constant
K12 PASS w=-0.166667, c_s^2=-0.166667 w=-1/6 exact, c_s^2<0 :: u=1/2 <=> w=-1/6 exactly (u=1+3w); a barotropic fluid then has c_s^2=-1/6 < 0 (unstable)
K13 PASS same source, u=0.500 vs 1.000 identical rho+3p, u differs by 2x :: the law fixes only rho+3p: two media with the same field have u=1/2 and u=1 -- u is underdetermined, not derived

  route (i) in one line: u = 1 + 3<w>; the law supplies the sum rho+3p, u needs the ratio p/rho.
  u=1/2 <=> <w>=-1/6 (tension of one sixth the energy density) -- a NEW PREMISE, not a derivation.

================================================================================================
K14-K15  ROUTE (ii) -- two-fluid: dust (w=0) + stiff (w=1)
================================================================================================
K14 PASS f_s=0.166667 (press) / -0.166667 (grav) 1/6 and -1/6 :: u=3f_s (pressure part) needs f_s=1/6; u=1+3f_s (whole gravity) needs f_s=-1/6 (unphysical); EQUAL densities (f_s=1/2) give u=1.50 or 2.50, never 1/2
K15 FAIL closest to 1/6: f_b at 0.0095 >0.008 (no framework number is 1/6) :: 3f_b=0.47138 matches u_data to -1.60 sigma -- the one numerical coincidence; 1 of 12 simple candidates land within 1 sigma

  f_b=0.15713  1/6=0.16667  |1/6-f_b|=0.00954  3f_b=0.47138  u_data=0.52351
  3f_b would be f_s = f_b (stiff fraction = cosmic baryon fraction): no mechanism, and it freezes u at 0.4714 at all masses, contradicting the theory's own u(M) running.

