K16-K17  ROUTE (iii) -- saturation: is u = mu(x=1), or 1-mu, or neither?
================================================================================================
K16 PASS mu(1)=1.6180, 1-mu=-0.6180 both >0.5 from 1/2 and from u_data; F(1/2)=1 :: neither: mu(x=1)=phi=1.6180, 1-mu=-0.6180. The law's exact 1/2 is M_ph/M_tot=1/2 at x=1/2 (y=1/2); at the anchors that fraction is 0.963 (MW) and 0.790 (cluster), not 1/2
K17 PASS lim(y->oo)=2.000000, lim(y->0)=1.000000, y_v: 1.0191/1.1230 2 and 1, anchors <1.15 :: the n=2 'half capacity' is a HIGH-acceleration statement (F1/F2 -> 2 as y->oo); in the deep limit the two laws coincide (->1) and at the anchors' y_v the ratio is 1.019 (MW) and 1.123 (cluster) -- the half capacity cannot supply u=1/2 where u lives

  response at x=1: mu=1.618034=phi, i.e. g(x=1)=1.5145e-10 m/s^2 = phi a0.
  The only exact 1/2 in the law is the local mass fraction M_ph/(M_b+M_ph)=1/2, at y=1/2 (r=sqrt(2) r_M).
  At r_v: MW y=0.001435 -> 0.9628; cluster y=0.055604 -> 0.7904.

